      "title": "Top Navigation",
      "description": "Leadership & Faculty | Bryant University Skip to Content Top Navigation Athletics Giving News Main navigation Discover Bryant Undergraduate Graduate Professional Education Discover Bryant Undergraduate Graduate Professional Education Top Navigation Mobile Athletics Giving News Vision 2030 Vision 2030, our strategic plan, is evolving the Bryant experience. Learn How About Bryant At a Glance Mission and History Leadership and Faculty Institutional Effectiveness and Strategy Initiatives AI at Bryant Centers and Institutes Global Advisory Council Sustainability at Bryant Wellbeing at Bryant Connect Partnering With Bryant Smithfield Resources Working at Bryant Contact Us Why Bryant We transform students into leaders with the drive, vision, and experience to leave a legacy. Learn How Career Outcomes Students achieve exceptional outcomes through career planning and the Amica Center for Career Education. Explore Your Path Our unique major-minor combination is a strength that leads to endless career possibilities. Explore Your Path Campus Life Bryant’s vibrant community is a transformative place to live and learn. Explore Campus Life Clubs and Organizations With over 100 student-run clubs, Bryant has something for everyone. Athletics Experience the competitive Bryant spirit firsthand through our athletic programs. Our Campus Residential Life Student Support Services Belonging and Wellbeing at Bryant New Student Programs Women’s Leadership at Bryant Campus Map Smithfield, RI, and Beyond Academics Discover your passions through Bryant’s interdisciplinary education. Academics Overview Experiential Learning Experiential education is at the core of your Bryant experience. Learn More Our Colleges College of Business College of Health and Behavioral Sciences College of Humanities and Social Sciences Learning at Bryant Explore our labs, faculty, and academic programs. Academic Departments Academic Labs General Education Curriculum Honors Program Our Faculty View Our Programs Admission Take your first step toward becoming a Bryant Bulldog. Learn More Application Info How to Apply Tuition and Financial Aid First-Year Students International Students Transfer Students Admitted Students Admitted Class Profile Take Action Apply Now Visit Campus Request Info Take Our Virtual Tour Precollege Summer Programs Important Dates Sun, Nov 01 Early Decision I Sun, Nov 15 Early Action Mon, Feb 01 Regular Decision Academics Our graduate programs offer an interdisciplinary education that prepares students for impactful careers. Learn More Our Faculty Our dedicated faculty members offer both industry expertise and personalized mentorship. Meet Our Faculty Our Programs Explore our nationally recognized graduate programs. All Programs MBAs Online Certificates Admission Advance your career through one of our nationally recognized programs. Learn More Application Info Tuition and Financial Aid International Students Important Dates Take Action Apply Now Request Info Contact Us Graduate Blog Important Dates Wed, Jul 15 On Campus Programs: Spring 2027 Priority Deadline View All Deadlines Self-Paced Learn anytime, anywhere with flexible self-paced courses. Instructor Led Expert-led courses offer structure, support, and results. Applied AI Academy Build the skills to leverage AI effectively in your role, team, and organization. Contact an Advisor Need some advice on next steps? Connect with a Bryant Course Advisor to help. Contact an Advisor View all Certificates Home Discover Bryant A New Era of Leadership Bryant University is a leader in providing transformational learning experiences, exceptional outcomes, and developing passionate, purpose-driven leaders. The university’s leadership team works toward a set of ambitious goals to cultivate academic excellence and student success. President Ross Gittell, Ph.D. Ross Gittell, Ph.D., one of the nation’s preeminent economists and economic development scholars, is the ninth president of Bryant University. Under his leadership, the institution is undergoing a bold new era of growth and innovation. Learn About President Gittell In This Section Sibling Nav AI at Bryant At a Glance Centers and Institutes Contact Us Global Advisory Council Leadership & Faculty External Conferences and Events Mission & History Office of Institutional Effectiveness & Strategy Smithfield Resources Sustainability Wellbeing at Bryant Working at Bryant Employee Directory Partnering With Bryant President’s Cabinet Bryant University’s senior leaders are drivers of change. They serve in an advisory capacity to the president, guide the university’s work, and inspire their teams to achieve positive change within the Bryant community. Inge-Lise Ameer Ed.D. Vice-President for Student Affairs and Dean of Students Gene Begin Chief Marketing Officer and Vice President for Communications Michelle L. Cloutier ’05MBA Vice President for Enrollment Management Chris Lehman MBA Chief Human Resources Officer and Vice President Donna Ng MBA Chief Financial Officer and Vice President for Business Affairs Rupendra Paliwal Ph.D. Provost and Chief Academic Officer Bill Smith J.D. Vice President Athletics and Recreation Edinaldo Tebaldi Ph.D. P'29 Vice President for Strategy and Partnerships David Wegrzyn ’86, P’23 Vice President for University Advancement Our Faculty View Faculty Our dedicated faculty provide an education that offers our students the knowledge and skills to thrive in an age of global complexity and change. Charles\n    Cullinan Ph D, MS, BS Professor Kevin\n    J.\n    Maloney Ph D, MA, BA Executive in Residence Suhong\n    Li Ph D, M Sc, BSBA Department Chair Information Systems and Analytics Elzotbek\n    Rustambekov Ph D, M Sc, MBA, BBA Department Chair Management Michael\n    Gravier Ph D, MS, BA Department Chair Marketing Christopher\n    Morse Ph D, MA, BA Department Chair Communication and Language Studies Amber\n    Day Ph D, MA, BA Department Chair History, Literature, and the Arts Gao\n 