    "https://news.bryant.edu/bryant-rises-9th-nationally-career-services-16th-best-run-college-2027-princeton-review-rankings": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Bryant rises to 9th nationally for career services, 16th best-run college in 2027 Princeton Review rankings | Bryant News Skip to Content Main navigation Bryant News Academics Community Global Students Alumni Bryant Magazine Media Academics Community Global Students Alumni Bryant Magazine Media Bryant rises to 9th nationally for career services, 16th best-run college in 2027 Princeton Review rankings Sep 03, 2026,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tby\n\t\t\t\tCasey Nilsson SMITHFIELD, R.I. — Bryant University rose to ninth in the nation for Best Career Services in The Princeton Review’s latest college rankings, joining a series of national distinctions for the university and its student experience. Bryant also debuted on several ranked lists this year, earning the 16 th spot for Best-Run Colleges, 16 th for Happiest Students, and 23 rd for Friendliest Students. The Douglas and Judith Krupp Library ranks 19 th nationally for Best College Library, and Bryant debuted at number seven for strong town relations. The university was once again named to The Princeton Review’s Best Value Colleges, Best Northeast, Green Colleges, and The Best 392 Colleges lists. “These rankings capture what distinguishes Bryant,” says President Ross Gittell, Ph.D. “Our students receive a transformative education, strong preparation for their careers, a deeply connected community where they can thrive, and a return on their educational investment in the top 1 percent nationally. Being named one of the nation’s best-run colleges is also a credit to the entire university and the collective commitment to student success and institutional excellence.” Bryant’s rise to ninth in the nation for Best Career Services marks a 16-spot increase from last year’s ranking. The Princeton Review bases its rankings on student assessments of their colleges’ career and job placement services. In their survey responses, Bryant students cited Bryant’s Amica Center for Career Education as one of the university’s greatest strengths. “The team in the career center does an excellent job helping students find job/internships and prepare for interviews,” one student told The Princeton Review. Others point to “so many great career networking opportunities” on and off campus. The Amica Center for Career Education works with students from their first year through Commencement, providing personalized career coaching, internship and employment support, mock interviews, resume assistance, career fairs, and connections with employers and alumni. First-year students begin that work through Bryant’s “Career “Students come to Bryant with big ambitions, hopes, and passions, and they find a community that supports them,” said Inge-Lise Ameer, Ed.D., vice president for student affairs and dean of students. “That happens through the career coaches, employer connections, internships, and careers upon graduation they find at the Amica Center, and through the friendships, mentors, organizations, and experiences that shape their lives on campus. These rankings are especially meaningful because they come directly from students and speak to the experience they have here.\" According to student respondents, “The Bryant community is very tight knit and helps make you feel at home on campus.” Students described their peers as “motivated, hardworking, kind, fun” and said that while Bryant students are driven, they support one another and “push each other to be better.” Students also described an active campus with a myriad of ways to get involved and meet people. One student said extracurricular activities “have introduced me to a new group of people and exposed me to new ways of thinking.” Another described Bryant as “extremely welcoming,” with the “perfect balance of academics, recreation, and extracurricular activities.” In their responses, students also illustrated a community of “different types of leaders who are each striving for their individual goals but are also devoted to maintaining a strong, cohesive student body.” Bryant’s seventh-in-the-nation ranking for town relations recognizes the university’s relationship with Smithfield and surrounding Rhode Island communities. Bryant students, faculty, and staff participate in community partnerships, events, and other programs throughout the region, including an annual Service Day when faculty and staff volunteer with local nonprofits and community organizations. The Princeton Review rankings follow other national recognitions for Bryant student outcomes. In August, LinkedIn ranked Bryant 41 st in the nation on its 2026 Top Colleges list, which recognizes 50 U.S. colleges for the long-term career success of their graduates. LinkedIn considers job placement, internship and recruiter demand, network strength, career advancement, and knowledge breadth. TIME also ranked Bryant in the top 100 nationally for career outcomes. No. 9 — Best Career Services No. 19 — Best College Library No. 16 — Best-Run Colleges No. 23 — Friendliest Students No. 16 — Happiest Students No. 7 — Town Relations Best Value Colleges Best Northeast Green Colleges The Best 392 Colleges About Bryant University For 163 years, Bryant University has been at the forefront of delivering an exceptional education that anticipates the future and prepares students to be innovative leaders of character in a changing world. The university delivers an integrated academic and student life experience, with nationally recognized academic programs at the intersection of business, liberal arts, and health and behavioral sciences, while embedding applied artificial intelligence and experiential learning across the curriculum. Located on a 465-acre contemporary campus in Smithfield, R.I., Bryant enrolls over 4,000 undergraduate and graduate students from 41 states and 50 countries. Bryant is recognized as a top one percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and is highly ranked by U.S. News and World Report , The Wall Street Journal , QS Stars, Money , Poets&Quants, and College Factual. Bryant.edu Read More Academics Campus Life Career ROI Student Success Related Stories Finding their freedom: New, first-of-its kind book helps teens struggling with an eating disorder Bryant’s Christina Tortolani, co-authors address eating disorder recovery gap through impactful resource At Convocation 2026, first-year students begin to ‘write the next chapter of Bryant University’ Campus community celebrates Class of 2030 in time-honored tradition Co-op programs give students extended experience in the workplace Six-month, full-time stints with employers offer undergrads more responsibility and leadership opportunities Bryant recognized for nationwide AI leadership by Center for Public Sector AI Center’s AI 50 names Bryant as only four-year university among this year’s organizational honorees What pension payout option should you choose? New research shows why health status matters ‘If the retiree is very healthy, then they may want to choose annuity,’ says Bryant’s Jessica Zhai, Ph.D. Bryant researcher examines how women, men respond to unequal workloads versus unequal earnings ‘Equipping managers with tools to identify and address workload disparities is essential,’ says Xiaofei Pan View More 1150 Douglas Pike, Smithfield, RI 02917 (401) 232-6000 Bryant Websites Bryant.edu Info Directory Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Bryant Bulldogs Publications Bryant Magazine Engage WJMF Privacy Policy Accessibility Emergency Information ©2026 The Trustees of Bryant University. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://news.bryant.edu/bryants-college-business-receives-high-marks-academic-experience-career-outcomes-2026-poetsquants": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Bryant’s College of Business receives high marks for academic experience, career outcomes in 2026 Poets&Quants survey | Bryant News Skip to Content Main navigation Bryant News Academics Community Global Students Alumni Bryant Magazine Media Academics Community Global Students Alumni Bryant Magazine Media Bryant’s College of Business receives high marks for academic experience, career outcomes in 2026 Poets&Quants survey Mar 30, 2026,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tby\n\t\t\t\tPeter Kerwin SMITHFIELD, RI—A year after initially breaking into the Poets&Quants survey of top undergraduate business schools in the country, Bryant University’s undergraduate College of Business was ranked #15 for academic experience and #45 for career outcomes in the 2026 survey. The national survey considers admissions standards, student feedback on academic experience, and career outcomes in determining the rankings. “Bryant continues to be recognized as a leader among the nation’s top undergraduate business schools, providing a transformational education that drives exceptional career outcomes,” says President Ross Gittell, Ph.D. “Our strong academic experience ranking is a testament to our faculty’s deep commitment to student outcomes and a curriculum that empowers students to think strategically, collaborate boldly, and lead with purpose.” “This survey is a recognition of intentional curriculum and learning experiences designed by our faculty, highlighting the success that comes from giving students the opportunity to tackle real-world challenges in an environment that fosters innovation and collaboration,” said Bryant’s Provost and Chief Academic Officer Rupendra Paliwal, Ph.D. “It’s about preparing students for what’s next, providing hands-on learning, global experiences, and high-tech tools that allow them to graduate as purpose-driven leaders ready to make a powerful impact from day one.” College of Business Dean Todd Alessandri, Ph.D., suggests the latest Poets&Quants findings are just the latest reminder of Bryant’s growing national and international standing. “Since Bryant’s notable emergence in the Poets&Quants rankings last year, the institution has continued to be recognized for our outstanding faculty and interdisciplinary learning approach that provides students with real-world experiences, analytical skills, and the confidence to know they are ready to achieve their career goals.” To learn more about Bryant’s College of Business, visit bryant.edu/college-business . About Bryant University For more than 160 years, Bryant University has been at the forefront of delivering an exceptional education that anticipates the future and prepares students to be innovative leaders of character in a changing world. The university delivers an integrated academic and student life experience with nationally recognized academic programs at the intersection of business, liberal arts, and health and behavioral sciences. Located on a 465-acre contemporary campus in Smithfield, R.I., Bryant enrolls approximately 3,800 undergraduate and graduate students from 41 states and 50 countries. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant.edu Read More Academics Career College of Business Experiential Learning President Provost ROI Related Stories Finding their freedom: New, first-of-its kind book helps teens struggling with an eating disorder Bryant’s Christina Tortolani, co-authors address eating disorder recovery gap through impactful resource At Convocation 2026, first-year students begin to ‘write the next chapter of Bryant University’ Campus community celebrates Class of 2030 in time-honored tradition Bryant rises to 9th nationally for career services, 16th best-run college in 2027 Princeton Review rankings University also earns national recognition for institutional excellence, student experience, academic resources Co-op programs give students extended experience in the workplace Six-month, full-time stints with employers offer undergrads more responsibility and leadership opportunities Bryant recognized for nationwide AI leadership by Center for Public Sector AI Center’s AI 50 names Bryant as only four-year university among this year’s organizational honorees What pension payout option should you choose? New research shows why health status matters ‘If the retiree is very healthy, then they may want to choose annuity,’ says Bryant’s Jessica Zhai, Ph.D. View More 1150 Douglas Pike, Smithfield, RI 02917 (401) 232-6000 Bryant Websites Bryant.edu Info Directory Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Bryant Bulldogs Publications Bryant Magazine Engage WJMF Privacy Policy Accessibility Emergency Information ©2026 The Trustees of Bryant University. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.bryant.edu/discover-bryant/centers-and-institutes/amica-center-career-education": {
      "title": "Amica Center for Career Education",
      "description": "Amica Center for Career Education | Bryant University We value your privacy We use cookies to enhance your browsing experience, serve personalized ads or content, and analyze our traffic. By clicking \"Accept All\", you consent to our use of cookies. Customize Reject All Accept All Customize Consent Preferences We use cookies to help you navigate efficiently and perform certain functions. You will find detailed information about all cookies under each consent category below. The cookies that are categorized as \"Necessary\" are stored on your browser as they are essential for enabling the basic functionalities of the site.... Show more Necessary Always Active Necessary cookies are required to enable the basic features of this site, such as providing secure log-in or adjusting your consent preferences. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable data. Cookie __cf_bm Duration 1 hour Description This cookie, set by Cloudflare, is used to support Cloudflare Bot Management. Cookie visid_incap_* Duration 1 year Description Incapsula sets this cookie to provide cloud-based website security services. Cookie incap_ses_* Duration session Description This is an Incapsula DDoS Protection and Web Application Firewall cookie that is used to relate HTTP requests to a certain session. Cookie _node Duration session Description No description available. Cookie _hash Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description No description available. Cookie PHPSESSID Duration session Description This cookie is native to PHP applications. The cookie stores and identifies a user's unique session ID to manage user sessions on the website. The cookie is a session cookie and will be deleted when all the browser windows are closed. Cookie ASLBSA Duration session Description No description available. Cookie ASLBSACORS Duration session Description No description available. Cookie ENCOMPASSCC_1434 Duration session Description Stores visitor consent preferences for cookies on the Bryant alumni portal, preserving chosen privacy settings across pages and future visits. Cookie ENCOMPASSSESSIONID_1434 Duration session Description Maintains secure session for Encompass login, enabling single sign-on and preserving authentication with return URL while navigating protected alumni pages. Cookie IGXSessionState Duration session Description No description available. Cookie _hr_suite_session_1 Duration 12 hours Description No description available. Cookie reese84 Duration 1 month Description No description available. Cookie _cookie_test Duration session Description Used by Goucher's application portal to verify cookie support, enable login redirects, and maintain session continuity during account access process. Cookie test Duration session Description No description available. Cookie VISITOR_PRIVACY_METADATA Duration 6 months Description YouTube sets this cookie to store the user's cookie consent state for the current domain. Cookie wpEmojiSettingsSupports Duration session Description WordPress sets this cookie when a user interacts with emojis on a WordPress site. It helps determine if the user's browser can display emojis properly. Cookie __RequestVerificationToken Duration session Description This cookie is set by web application built in ASP.NET MVC Technologies. This is an anti-forgery cookie used for preventing cross site request forgery attacks. Cookie rc::a Duration Never Expires Description This cookie is set by the Google recaptcha service to identify bots to protect the website against malicious spam attacks. Cookie rc::c Duration session Description This cookie is set by the Google recaptcha service to identify bots to protect the website against malicious spam attacks. Cookie OptanonConsent Duration 1 year Description OneTrust sets this cookie to store details about the site's cookie category and check whether visitors have given or withdrawn consent from the use of each category. Cookie OptanonAlertBoxClosed Duration 1 year Description OneTrust sets this cookie to allow it to set cookies based on the user's consent and hide the cookies banner once the user has read and acknowledged it. Cookie TiPMix Duration 1 hour Description The TiPMix cookie is set by Azure to determine which web server the users must be directed to. Cookie x-ms-routing-name Duration 1 hour Description Azure sets this cookie for routing production traffic by specifying the production slot. Cookie .AspNetCore.Antiforgery.* Duration session Description This cookie is set by Microsoft AspNet for the purpose of Anti-forgery protection. Cookie DBMS_RETURNURL_* Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description This cookie is used to store the URL of the page a user was attempting to access before being redirected Cookie __Secure-ENID Duration 1 year 1 month Description The __Secure-ENID cookie is a type of secure cookie used for authentication and to ensure the security of user sessions. Cookie cookietest Duration session Description The cookietest cookie is typically used to determine whether the user's browser accepts cookies, essential for website functionality and user experience. Cookie aa-cookie-test Duration session Description Description is currently not available. Cookie cookieyes-* Duration 1 year Description CookieYes sets this cookie for consent solution management. Functional Functional cookies help perform certain functionalities like sharing the content of the website on social media platforms, collecting feedback, and other third-party features. Cookie _gcl_au Duration 3 months Description Google Tag Manager sets this cookie to experiment advertisement efficiency of websites using their services. Cookie li_gc Duration 6 months Description Linkedin set this cookie for storing visitor's consent regarding using cookies for non-essential purposes. Cookie lidc Duration 1 day 1 minute Description LinkedIn sets the lidc cookie to facilitate data center selection. Cookie CDNPHPSESSID Duration session Description Stores a temporary session identifier enabling YouVisit embedded tour features, preserving user interactions, preferences, and state across pages during visits. Cookie Stl_Launch Duration session Description Stores site configuration and campaign launch preferences, enabling correct loading of planned giving features and persisting user choices across visits. Cookie Stl_Org Duration 2 hours Description Stores the nonprofit’s identifier and site settings to deliver correct branding, content, and seamless navigation across planned giving website sections. Cookie bgColor Duration session Description No description available. Cookie bp_plack_session Duration session Description Stores temporary session data to maintain advanced search filters, pagination, and browsing preferences across Whitworth Digital Commons honors repository pages. Cookie VISITOR_INFO1_LIVE Duration 6 months Description A cookie set by YouTube to measure bandwidth that determines whether the user gets the new or old player interface. Cookie ytidb::LAST_RESULT_ENTRY_KEY Duration Never Expires Description The cookie ytidb::LAST_RESULT_ENTRY_KEY is used by YouTube to store the last search result entry that was clicked by the user. This information is used to improve the user experience by providing more relevant search results in the future. Cookie mid Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description The mid cookie is set by Instagram to personalize user experience by remembering user preferences and settings. Cookie navigationCache Duration 15 minutes Description Stores cached navigation data to speed page loads, remember topbar state, and persist menu preferences and recent links across sessions. Analytics Analytical cookies are used to understand how visitors interact with the website. These cookies help provide information on metrics such as the number of visitors, bounce rate, traffic source, etc. Cookie _ga_* Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store and count page views. Cookie _ga Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to calculate visitor, session and campaign data and track site usage for the site's analytics report. The cookie stores information anonymously and assigns a randomly generated number to recognize unique visitors. Cookie nmstat Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description This cookie is set by SiteImprove. This cookie is used for web analytics, the cookie contain a ID string about the session. The cookie records the visitor use of the website. This information is used to improve the site experience.The cookie does not contain any personal information. Cookie _gid Duration 1 day Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store information on how visitors use a website while also creating an analytics report of the website's performance. Some of the collected data includes the number of visitors, their source, and the pages they visit anonymously. Cookie _gat_UA-* Duration 1 minute Description Google Analytics sets this cookie for user behavior tracking. Cookie gpv_evar7 Duration 1 hour Description Stores the previous value of an Adobe Analytics eVar to track changes between pages for journey analysis, attribution, and reporting. Cookie gpv_evar8 Duration 1 hour Description Stores the previous value of Adobe Analytics eVar 8 across pages to analyze navigation sequences, attribution changes, and behavior trends. Cookie bp_visitor_id Duration 3 minutes Description Assigns a unique visitor identifier to measure usage, track article and page interactions, and compile readership analytics across repository content. Cookie original_referer Duration 2 minutes Description Stores the initial referring URL that brought visitors to the site, supporting attribution, analytics, campaign measurement, and redirect or navigation. Cookie YSC Duration session Description YSC cookie is set by Youtube and is used to track the views of embedded videos on Youtube pages. Cookie s_ips Duration session Description Adobe Analytics sets this cookie to store information required by the getPercentPageViewed plugin. Cookie s_tp Duration session Description Adobe Analytics sets this cookie to know how much of the page you viewed. Cookie s_ppv Duration session Description The cookie is used to determine the percentage of the page that has been displayed to the user. Cookie s_cc Duration session Description Adobe Analytics sets this cookie to determine whether or not cookies are enabled in the user's browser. Cookie s_ecid Duration 2 years Description Adobe installs this cookie to allow persistent ID tracking in the 1st party state and is used as a reference ID if the AMCV cookie has expired. Cookie ai_session Duration 1 hour Description This is a unique anonymous session identifier cookie set by Microsoft Application Insights software to gather statistical usage and telemetry data for apps built on the Azure cloud platform. Cookie _gat_gtag_UA_* Duration 1 minute Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store a unique user ID. Cookie _gat_* Duration 1 minute Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to throttle the request rate. Cookie ___utmvc Duration Less than a minute Description The ___utmvc cookie is installed by Google Analytics to gather data on the user's site usage. This data is then used to compile reports and improve the site. Cookie _session_id Duration session Description _session_id cookie stores a unique identifier for a user's session, allowing servers to identify and track user activities within a website or application. Cookie amplitude_id_* Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Amplitude sets this cookie, which is used to uniquely identify the user's machine. Cookie amplitude_cookie_test Duration session Description Amplitude sets this cookie, which is used to uniquely identify the user's machine. Cookie __scuuid Duration 1 year Description Stores a unique visitor identifier for the SureCatch embed, enabling session continuity, lead capture analytics, and on-site engagement across visits. Cookie __scuuid_h Duration 1 year Description Used by SureCatch embed to assign a unique visitor ID, track interactions across sessions, improve lead capture performance and analytics. Cookie _clck Duration 1 year Description Microsoft Clarity sets this cookie to retain the browser's Clarity User ID and settings exclusive to that website. This guarantees that actions taken during subsequent visits to the same website will be linked to the same user ID. Cookie _clsk Duration 1 day 1 minute Description Microsoft Clarity sets this cookie to store and consolidate a user's pageviews into a single session recording. Cookie SM Duration session Description Microsoft Clarity cookie set this cookie for synchronizing the MUID across Microsoft domains. Cookie MR Duration 7 days 1 minute Description This cookie, set by Bing, is used to collect user information for analytics purposes. Cookie s_sq Duration session Description This is an Adobe Analytics cookie that contains information about the previous link that was clicked on by the user. Performance Performance cookies are used to understand and analyze the key performance indexes of the website which helps in delivering a better user experience for the visitors. Cookie AWSALBCORS Duration 7 days 1 minute Description Amazon Web Services set this cookie for load balancing. Cookie AWSALB Duration 7 days 1 minute Description AWSALB is an application load balancer cookie set by Amazon Web Services to map the session to the target. Cookie B100Serverpoolcookie Duration session Description No description available. Cookie TEST_AMCV_COOKIE_WRITE Duration session Description Used by Adobe Launch to test whether browsers permit setting the Experience Cloud visitor cookie, enabling analytics, segmentation, and personalization. Cookie akaalb_charitablegift_ALB Duration session Description Supports DAF Direct charitable giving widget by providing load balancing and session stickiness, ensuring reliable loads and consistent donor experiences. Cookie JSESSIONID Duration session Description New Relic uses this cookie to store a session identifier so that New Relic can monitor session counts for an application. Cookie nlbi_* Duration session Description The Hotels Network sets this cookie to improve security and provide load-balancing to ensure that a client's requests are sent to the same origin server. Cookie AMCV_*AdobeOrg Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Adobe-Dtm sets this cookie to find the unique user ID that recognizes the user on returning visits. Cookie AMCVS_*AdobeOrg Duration session Description Adobe-Dtm sets this cookie to store a unique ID to identify a unique visitor. Cookie s_pers Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description The s_pers cookie is set by Adobe for anonymized identification of new visitors, to help analyze clickstream data, and track historical activity on the website. Cookie s_sess Duration session Description This is a Adobe Site Catalyst cookie. This cookie is used to collect information on how visitors use the website and this information is used for improving the website. Cookie _uetsid Duration 1 day Description Bing Ads sets this cookie to engage with a user that has previously visited the website. Cookie _uetvid Duration 1 year 24 days Description Bing Ads sets this cookie to engage with a user that has previously visited the website. Cookie SRM_B Duration 1 year 24 days 1 minute Description Used by Microsoft Advertising as a unique ID for visitors. Advertisement Advertisement cookies are used to provide visitors with customized advertisements based on the pages you visited previously and to analyze the effectiveness of the ad campaigns. Cookie __spdt Duration 1 year Description Enables Spotify's pixel to collect analytics on site visits, interactions, and conversions, optimizing advertising campaigns and user experience and personalization. Cookie BCTempID Duration 11 minutes Description No description available. Cookie ttcsid Duration 3 months Description Stores a session identifier for TikTok Pixel to measure site interactions, attribute ad conversions, optimize campaigns, and support audience retargeting. Cookie test_cookie Duration 15 minutes Description doubleclick.net sets this cookie to determine if the user's browser supports cookies. Cookie _fbp Duration 3 months Description Facebook sets this cookie to store and track interactions. Cookie _ttp Duration 3 months Description TikTok set this cookie to track and improve the performance of advertising campaigns, as well as to personalize the user experience. Cookie IDE Duration 1 year 24 days 1 minute Description Google DoubleClick IDE cookies store information about how the user uses the website to present them with relevant ads according to the user profile. Cookie _tt_enable_cookie Duration 3 months Description Tiktok set this cookie to collect data about behavior and activities on the website and to measure the effectiveness of the advertising. Cookie ttcsid_* Duration 3 months Description TikTok sets this cookie as a session identification cookie to support user tracking and session continuity across a website. Cookie bcookie Duration 1 year Description LinkedIn sets this cookie from LinkedIn share buttons and ad tags to recognize browser IDs. Cookie BCSessionID Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days 1 minute Description Blueconic sets this cookie as a unique identifier for the BlueConic profile. Cookie _hashV Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Stores a hashed visitor identifier to preserve portal preferences, attribute marketing campaigns, and optimize campus-visit scheduling, analytics, and user experience. Cookie cu Duration 1 year Description No description available. Cookie __Secure-YNID Duration 6 months Description YouTube cookie used to protect user security and prevent fraud, especially during the login process. Cookie __Secure-ROLLOUT_TOKEN Duration 6 months Description YouTube sets this cookie to manage feature rollout and experimentation. It helps Google control which new features or interface changes are shown to users as part of testing and staged rollouts, ensuring consistent experience for a given user during an experiment. Cookie __Secure-YEC Duration past Description Description is currently not available. Cookie demdex Duration 6 months Description The demdex cookie, set under the domain demdex.net, is used by Adobe Audience Manager to help identify a unique visitor across domains. Cookie dpm Duration 6 months Description The dpm cookie, set under the Demdex domain, assigns a unique ID to each visiting user, hence allowing third-party advertisers to target these users with relevant ads. Cookie everest_g_v2 Duration 1 year Description The cookie is set under the everesttech.net domain to map clicks to other events on the client's website. Cookie everest_session_v2 Duration session Description This cookie, set by Everesttech, is used for targeted ads and to document efficacy of each individual ad. Cookie ai_user Duration 1 year Description Microsoft Azure sets this cookie as a unique user identifier cookie, enabling counting of the number of users accessing the application over time. Cookie MUID Duration 1 year 24 days 1 minute Description Bing sets this cookie to recognize unique web browsers visiting Microsoft sites. This cookie is used for advertising, site analytics, and other operations. Cookie NID Duration 6 months Description Google sets the cookie for advertising purposes; to limit the number of times the user sees an ad, to unwanted mute ads, and to measure the effectiveness of ads. Cookie ANONCHK Duration 11 minutes Description The ANONCHK cookie, set by Bing, is used to store a user's session ID and verify ads' clicks on the Bing search engine. The cookie helps in reporting and personalization as well. Uncategorised Other uncategorized cookies are those that are being analyzed and have not been classified into a category as yet. No cookies to display. Reject All S"
